<title>UK: Aluminium stocks fell in July - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks fell in July - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.342 million tonnes at the end of July 1996, compared with 3.375 million in June and 3.808 million in July 1995, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.818 million tonnes versus 1.819 million and 2.171 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Jul 96   Jun 96    Jul 95</p>
<p>    Africa		    74	 67	  57</p>
<p>    North America	1,612    1,630     1,823</p>
<p>    Latin America	  190	183	 190</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	154	160	 171</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,185    1,203     1,404</p>
<p>    Oceania		  127	132	 163</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   JUL 96    JUN 96    JUL 95</p>
<p>    Africa		   30	  28	  28</p>
<p>    North America	 759	 747	 904</p>
<p>    Latin America	 146	 133	 134</p>
<p>    East/South Asia     125	 132	 143</p>
<p>    Europe		  665	 680	 853</p>
<p>    Oceania		  93	  99	 109</p>
</text>
